Article 8 In any of the following circumstances, letter of credit fraud shall be found to exist:
(1) the beneficiary forges documents or submits documents with false contents;
(2) the beneficiary maliciously fails to deliver goods or delivers goods of no value;
(3) the beneficiary colludes with the applicant or any other third party to submit false documents without a genuine underlying transaction; or
(4) other circumstances constituting letter of credit fraud.

Article 10 Where a People's Court finds that letter of credit fraud exists, it shall rule to suspend payment or adjudge to terminate payment of the amount under the letter of credit, except in any of the following circumstances:
(1) the nominee or authorized person of the issuing bank has made payment in good faith in accordance with the instructions of the issuing bank;
(2) the issuing bank or its nominee or authorized person has accepted the bills or documents under the letter of credit in good faith;
(3) the confirming bank has performed its obligation of payment in good faith; or
(4) the negotiating bank has negotiated in good faith.

Article 11 Where a party applies before prosecution for suspension of payment of the amount under a letter of credit and satisfies the following conditions, the People's Court shall accept it:
(1) the People's Court accepting the application has jurisdiction over the letter of credit dispute case;
(2) the evidence materials provided by the applicant prove the existence of circumstances under Article 8 of these Provisions;
(3) if measures to suspend payment of the amount under the letter of credit are not taken, the applicant's lawful rights and interests would suffer irreparable harm;
(4) the applicant has provided reliable and sufficient security; and
(5) none of the circumstances under Article 10 of these Provisions exists.
Where a party applies during litigation for suspension of payment of the amount under a letter of credit, it shall satisfy the conditions stipulated in items (2), (3), (4), and (5) of the preceding paragraph.
